WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.302
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.603
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.172
between Doritos in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.841
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.746
In the UK, Doritos come
in four portion sizes,

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.714
starting with this one,
which is a 30-gram bag.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.750
However, these only come
in the form of multipacks,

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.318
either as a multipack of five

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:20.020
or as a multipack of 12.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.188
The smallest bag of Doritos
you can get in the US

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:25.058
is the multipack size,
which is this, 1 ounce.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:28.094
You can get these in multipacks of 10.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.031
Next up we have a grab
bag, which is 48 grams.

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.232
These are usually found as part of

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.234
a lunchtime meal deal, just as a snack.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.237
Next size up, a 1 3/4 size bag.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.440
Next size up, this is
the 2 3/4 pounds bag.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.741
Next up we have our regular bag,

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.943
which in the UK is 180 grams.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:44.778
That's nothing.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:49.482
Our standard bag size, 9.75 ounces.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.617
Finally, we have our biggest size,

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.353
which is a share-size bag
coming in at 230 grams.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.988
We got you beat again, UK.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:59.159
This is our party pack, 14.5 ounces,

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.828
which is also 411 grams.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.964
88% larger than any
size you have in the UK.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.332
Let's count out all the Doritos

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.600
in our respective largest bags

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.768
to see what the difference looks like.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.870
The good news is that I'm
counting out this bag,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.439
which is 230 grams.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:15.909
Joe is counting out a
party-sized bag of American ones,

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.844
which is 425 grams,

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.012
so he might be here a while.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.046
Sorry, Joe.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.147
Yeah, thanks, Harry.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:28.688
[sighs]

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:36.062
Joe: We're doing the math so
all you stoners don't have to.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.499
15 times 8.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.471
11 times 10, plus 1, 2, 3.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:47.474
Count out, like, 10 chips, weigh them,

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.809
divide by 10, and then go, OK,

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.011
that's how much a chip on average weighs,

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.913
and then weigh the pile of crumbs

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:54.914
and divide it by that number,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:55.915
seeing how many chips are –

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:56.749
does that make sense?

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.052
I'm gonna be here all day.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:02.455
So, one chip weighs 2.5 grams.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.191
So the remainder of the crumbs,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.127
65 grams.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.362
What's 65 divided by 2.5?

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.899
So, altogether, 168 chips.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.768
Wow, we're really smart.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.270
That was smart what we
just did there, right?

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:18.505
Nine.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.242
Leaving our total at 119 Doritos.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.144
My flatmates can eat these.

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:27.647
I won't tell them the amount
of fondling that's gone on.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.051
Here's everything that's
in a Cool Original Dorito

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:32.886
in the UK.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.521
Corn (maize), vegetable oils

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.189
(sunflower and rapeseed
in various proportions),

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:39.125
[Harry talking over himself]

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:48.201
And here's everything in a
Cool Ranch Dorito in the US.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.035
All right.

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.437
Corn; vegetable oil,
which is corn, canola,

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.807
and/or sunflower oil;
maltodextrin (made from corn).

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.109
A lot of corn in these chips.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:59.479
[Joe talking over himself]

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.424
There are a few things
to watch out for in here

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.092
as well as in other Dorito flavors.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.395
Ah, good old USA-only food coloring,

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.597
Red 40 and Yellow No. 5.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:18.631
It's in everything these days.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:22.168
And the UK, of course,
opts to color its Doritos

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.237
with things like annatto and paprika.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.939
A fun one to know is that
the Doritos in the UK

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.107
and the US both contain
potassium chloride.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.943
Now, in normal doses,
this is perfectly normal

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.444
and safe to eat in food,

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.713
as it's used to reduce the
sodium content in salt.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.715
However, it's also one
of the three drugs used

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.483
in a three-drug cocktail of chemicals

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.952
used for lethal injections.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.386
Enough potassium chloride will increase

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.021
your blood's concentration of potassium,

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.356
which will create an irregular heartbeat

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.791
and lead to cardiac arrest.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.726
Ah, how many Doritos would
it take to kill someone?

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.528
I think just one, if you crush it up,

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.964
put in a syringe, and just
jam it right into the arm.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.699
Death by Cool Ranch.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.766
That's how I want to go.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.669
I've eaten five of these,

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.705
and I feel like I'm gonna die.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.542
This here is 100 grams
of Cool Ranch Doritos.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:05.945
And in the US, that contains 535 calories.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:09.382
The total fat is 28.56 grams,

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:13.586
sodium 678.3 milligrams. Oof.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.355
That's a lot of sodium
in that pile right there.

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.257
We actually call those
Cool Original over here

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.658
because no one in the
UK knows what ranch is.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.360
But as far as we're
aware, they are the same.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.829
In the UK, 100 grams of
Cool Original Doritos

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.597
contains 498 calories,

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.266
25.5 grams of fat,

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.301
592 milligrams of sodium,

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.836
and 58.1 grams of carbs.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.205
So our version has slightly more calories,

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:34.574
fat, and sodium than the UK version.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.009
What about the least healthy flavor?

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.710
Well, in the UK, Flame Grilled Steak

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.545
is the highest in calories and sodium.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.114
Four Flame Grilled Steak grab bags

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.448
would be your entire daily allowance

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.284
of fat, sodium, and calories.

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:46.319
"With intense flavours, full-on crunch,

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:49.055
and a Grilled Steak Kick,
Doritos are the great tasting

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.758
bold snack for when you're
getting together with mates!"

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:55.261
Bold of you to assume I'm
sharing these with my friends.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.996
What about the least healthiest Dorito?

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.731
Well, the calorie count
is pretty much similar

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.300
among all of them, but if
you're paying attention

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.869
to your sodium intake,
which I guess you should be,

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:04.737
then I would say steer clear of

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.373
the Spicy Sweet Chili Doritos.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:10.276
100 grams of these,

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.078
so roughly two of these,

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:16.149
is 963.9 milligrams of sodium.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:19.118
That is a 42% increase
from the Cool Ranch.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:22.221
[crunching]

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:26.326
Everything tastes like insanity.

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.094
I don't mind this, but you gotta, like,

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.929
water them down or something, Doritos.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.564
This is way too strong.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.432
Yet, I'm eating them.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.601
Here are all the Doritos
you'll find in the UK

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.003
that you won't find in the US.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.072
And here are most of the Doritos

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.406
that are native to the US.

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:41.774
Let's start with the classics.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:44.444
In the UK, you will find Guacamole flavor,

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:45.978
Flame Grilled Steak flavor,

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.381
Lightly Salted, and Hint of Lime Doritos.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.649
Then we have a few
which aren't technically

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.017
exclusives but have some differences,

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.218
which I thought were worth pointing out.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.953
For example, as I previously mentioned,

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.589
we call these ones Cool
Original instead of Cool Ranch,

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:57.690
because ranch just really isn't

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.258
a popular condiment in the UK.

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:01.427
There are also a couple of
color differences worth noting.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:03.363
For example, the red ones in the UK

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.664
are actually Chilli Heatwave,

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:07.767
whereas the bright orange
ones are Tangy Cheese.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.570
In the UK, Doritos also
offers a range of salsas

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.306
and other dips, like nacho
cheese and sour cream.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.708
In the UK, you are actively
encouraged by Doritos,

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:16.909
and society as a whole,

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.778
to dip your Doritos into these sauces,

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.513
as you can see on the packaging here.

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:22.281
But apparently Americans
find that super weird

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.317
and will only ever dip
plain chips into salsa.

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:25.017
Is that right, Joe?

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:30.056
Doritos and dips seems like flavor mayhem.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:34.193
The thought of dipping
Nacho Cheese Doritos

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.194
into nacho cheese,

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.897
I think one bite would just
unplug you from the matrix.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:41.067
That seems, like, impossible to handle.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.602
But, yeah, go for it.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:46.272
Sweaty hands. Sweaty Dorito hands.

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:48.207
Save my pride.

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.177
That's really on there.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.211
I have no grip strength.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.613
Oh, wow.

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.581
Before, you know, I've
loosened it up for you.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:57.650
There we go.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:58.484
Nice.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:06:59.719
Every episode.

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.921
I need to work on my grip
strength, go climbing.

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:03.723
To me, it's just like that
scene in "Ratatouille"

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.892
where Remy is feeding his
brother a piece of cheese

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:06.959
and a piece of strawberry,

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:08.895
and if you eat them one at
a time, they're pretty good.

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:10.363
But if you mix them together ...

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:12.732
[dynamic music]

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:16.035
It's a taste explosion.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.937
Delicious! Why wouldn't you do this?

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:18.905
You guys are missing out, OK?

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:19.839
You're missing out.

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:22.208
I don't think I'm missing
out. I think that seems like

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:24.710
way more flavor than I
can handle, personally.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.178
Enjoy!

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:28.114
So, they got the Tapatio flavored Dorito.

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:29.449
Collab, love to see it.

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:32.485
This guy's Salsa Verde.

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:33.586
Spicy Nacho.

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:35.822
Spicy Sweet Chili, we saw
that a little bit earlier.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:37.356
This one, the Flamas!

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.692
Just look at the fire on
that. These gotta be hot.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:40.893
Whoa.

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:43.362
Uh-oh, I don't like the look of this chip.

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:46.599
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:48.534
I would say that the Flamas flavor

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.336
reminds me a lot of Takis.

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:53.239
But if that's not Taki enough for you –

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:56.008
and this, I think, is
actually really irritating –

00:07:56.008 --> 00:08:00.112
Doritos also has something
called the Dinamitas.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:01.547
What do those look like?

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:02.381
Takis.

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.550
Doritos, come on, guys.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.453
Let another company make some money.

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:10.923
Takis are better.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.292
Two other US exclusives that
I could not get my hands on

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:14.760
by the filming of this episode

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.662
is Blazin' Buffalo &amp; Ranch

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.030
and Poppin' Jalapeno.

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:20.266
What appears to be, I don't know,

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:21.968
an attempt at making a healthier Dorito,

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:23.002
if there's such a thing.

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:26.138
So, White Cheddar and Spicy White Cheddar.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:28.674
"At Simply, our snacks
are made with ingredients

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:32.078
you can feel good about and
come from the brands you love.

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:34.247
We call it PURE DELICIOUSNESS."

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:35.181
Barf!

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:37.617
Ingredients: organic corn,

00:08:37.617 --> 00:08:40.453
organic expeller-pressed sunflower oil,

00:08:40.453 --> 00:08:42.655
organic cheddar cheese,
milk, cheese culture solids,

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:44.757
enzymes, organic maltodextrin.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.425
They just put the word organic
in front of everything.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:49.295
Organic maltodextrin
made from corn, sea salt,

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:52.598
organic butter, cream,
salt, organic skim milk,

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:56.135
organic spices, citric
acid, organic garlic powder.

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:58.971
So I think these are
more organic. [laughs]

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:02.041
You know what they taste like? Sunchips.

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:03.009
I hate Sunchips.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:04.777
We also have an exclusive Dorito shape,

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:06.245
which is Doritos Stax.

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:08.481
These are kind of like
a Dorito-Pringle hybrid,

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:10.249
which are mostly just
like regular Doritos,

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:11.584
but then stacked in a triangular tube.

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:13.452
Yo!

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:14.687
Doritos is going after Takis,

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:15.655
now they're going after Pringles?

00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:18.824
Doritos, let someone else
make a dollar in this space!

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:20.960
These come in four flavors,
and we've got them all here.

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:23.663
We've got a Mexican Chilli Salsa Stax,

00:09:23.663 --> 00:09:25.298
these Flaming Chicken Wings Stax,

00:09:25.298 --> 00:09:26.732
some Sour Cream &amp; Onion Stax,

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:28.367
and Ultimate Cheese Stax.

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.670
Yeah, I mean, they kind of look like

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.605
maybe thinner than normal Doritos.

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:34.674
I wonder why these are Ultimate Cheese

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:36.375
compared to just our normal Tangy Cheese.

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:37.410
Let's find out.

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:39.478
Those aren't bad.

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:40.546
They're pretty good, they're pretty good.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.181
That is an exclusive container shape,

00:09:42.181 --> 00:09:44.283
but in the US, we have
an exclusive chip shape.

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:47.219
And that is these, the 3D Crunch.

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:50.389
Two flavors that we got are Spicy Ranch.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:51.223
Spicy Ranch?

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:52.124
I think I'm in trouble.

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:55.094
And Chili Cheese Nacho.

00:09:56.896 --> 00:09:59.899
I like it. They're,
like, lighter, fluffier.

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:02.268
Let me ask you guys a question.

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:03.836
What shape does that look like?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.705
Think really hard.

00:10:05.705 --> 00:10:08.574
Announcer: Live from New
York, it's "What Shape Is It?"

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:10.276
What does this shape look like?

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:11.911
Imagine if it didn't
close up at the bottom.

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:15.348
This looks exactly like a Bugle!

00:10:15.348 --> 00:10:17.783
Doritos is going after everyone.

00:10:19.185 --> 00:10:21.354
That's why I like them so
much, they taste like Bugles.

00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:23.456
Stay out of Bugles' lane, Doritos.

00:10:23.456 --> 00:10:24.924
You got a lot to learn.

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:26.926
You got a lot to learn about Bugles.

00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:29.528
And you got a lot to learn about Takis.

00:10:29.528 --> 00:10:31.597
Actually, these guys are
kind of growing on me.

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:34.734
Overall though, yeah.

00:10:34.734 --> 00:10:35.534
I like Doritos.

